ns in the given array.\n    An inversion is a pair (i, j) such that i < j and arr[i] > arr[j].\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _merge_sort_and_count(sub_arr: List[int]) -> Tuple[List[int], int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursively sorts the array and counts inversions using a modified merge sort.\n        Returns the sorted array and the inversion count.\n        \"\"\"\n        n = len(sub_arr)\n        if n <= 1:\n            return sub_arr, 0\n\n        mid = n // 2\n        left_half, left_inversions = _merge_sort_and_count(sub_arr[:mid])\n        right_half, right_inversions = _merge_sort_and_count(sub_arr[mid:])\n\n        merged_arr = []\n        i = j = 0\n        split_inversions = 0\n\n        while i < len(left_half) and j < len(right_half):\n            if left_half[i] <= right_half[j]:\n                merged_arr.append(left_half[i])\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                split_inversions += len(left_half) - i\n                merged_arr.append(right_half[j])\n                j += 1\n\n        merged_arr.extend(left_half[i:])\n        merged_arr.extend(right_half[j:])\n\n        return merged_arr, left_inversions + right_inversions + split_inversions\n\n    # Create a copy to ensure the original input array is not modified.\n    _, count = _merge_sort_and_count(list(arr))\n    return count", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}, {"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "def get_Inv_Count(arr):\n    \"\"\"Counts inversions in an array using a modified merge sort algorithm.\n    An inversion is a pair (i, j) such that i < j and arr[i] > arr[j].\"\"\"\n\n    def _merge_sort_and_count(original_arr_copy, left, right):\n        \"\"\"Recursively sorts a sub-array segment and counts inversions within it.\n        Returns total inversions and the sorted sub-array.\"\"\"\n        if left >= right:\n            # Base case: empty or single-element sub-array.\n            return 0, original_arr_copy[left : right + 1]\n\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n\n        # Recursively count inversions in left and right halves.\n        left_inversions, left_sorted_arr = _merge_sort_and_count(original_arr_copy, left, mid)\n        right_inversions, right_sorted_arr = _merge_sort_and_count(original_arr_copy, mid + 1, right)\n\n        # Count split inversions and merge the two sorted halves.\n        split_inversions, merged_sorted_arr = _merge_and_count_split_inversions(\n            left_sorted_arr, right_sorted_arr\n        )\n\n        total_inversions = left_inversions + right_inversions + split_inversions\n        return total_inversions, merged_sorted_arr\n\n    def _merge_and_count_split_inversions(left_arr, right_arr):\n        \"\"\"Merges two sorted arrays and counts inversions between them.\n        Returns split inversions count and the merged sorted array.\"\"\"\n        merged_arr = []\n        i, j = 0, 0\n        split_inversions = 0\n\n        while i < len(left_arr) and j < len(right_arr):\n            if left_arr[i] <= right_arr[j]:\n                merged_arr.append(left_arr[i])\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                # If right_arr[j] is smaller, it forms inversions with remaining elements in left_arr.\n                merged_arr.append(right_arr[j])\n                split_inversions += (len(left_arr) - i)\n                j += 1\n\n        # Append any remaining elements from either list.\n        merged_arr.extend(left_arr[i:])\n        merged_arr.extend(right_arr[j:])\n\n        return split_inversions, merged_arr\n    \n    # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original array if passed by reference.\n    # The helper function returns the sorted array, but only the count is required by the caller.\n    \n    # Handle edge case for empty or single-element arrays\n    if not arr or len(arr) < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    inversions, _ = _merge_sort_and_count(list(arr), 0, len(arr) - 1)\n    return inversions", "base_status": "pas